From 9de610ac48893609d98fe18207c3f048b978d43a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Quintin Smits <qd.smits@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 00:35:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] feat(tools): a form mill kind with roundover, cove, ogee,
 V-groove and bead presets

Add ToolKind::FormMill (file word form_mill). Its cutting edge is the
outline in Tool::form (points [z, r, arc], a pilot length and the preset
that wrote them). The presets write the outline from router bit
catalogue numbers; the pilot band does not cut. The outline sets the
diameter and the flute length. An undercut outline is refused by name
(#896). Tool::meridian and Tool::profile read the outline; the operation
stamp hashes it.

Every operation refuses a form mill by name (it is in the CONE family
for the edge form work), and the 2D Chamfer names that work. The
catalog gets a roundover, a cove and a V-groove bit in mm and inch. The
tool editor has the kind, a Form preset list with its number rows and
the pilot length; MCP add_tool and edit_tool take the form. No file
version step: an older build refuses the form_mill word by name.

Fixes #3369

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
