From 5b5cba7681f3c7b80a8a45cca5cf710c8ee67e2c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 17:42:23 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] fix(mcp): edit_tool refuses a form mill value that
 settling replaces

Review of #3946, finding 1. A patch that states a diameter, a flute
length or outline points that the form outline or its preset then
replaces is refused by the field's name. It is no longer dropped with a
success. One rule covers each patched key: the stated tool is compared
with the settled tool. A preset number edit still settles.

The Draw cutter view shows a form mill's diameter and flute length and
takes no typing there, as the Tool tab does.

Refs #3369

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
